Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No third-party source code is vendored in this repository. The dependencies
listed below must be installed separately before use and are governed by their
respective licenses.

Python packages (pip):
  numpy       BSD 3-Clause          - compatible with Apache-2.0 distribution
  Pillow      MIT-CMU               - compatible with Apache-2.0 distribution
  mlx-whisper (optional)  MIT       - only if you use speech transcription.
                                      Apple Silicon only.
  pyobjc-framework-Vision / pyobjc-framework-Cocoa (optional)  MIT
    - macOS only, for on-screen text via Apple Vision. PyObjC components such
      as libffi have separate license terms; consult the installed packages.

External executables (outside Python):
  ffmpeg / ffprobe
    ffmpeg is LGPL or GPL depending on how it was built. Inspect the installed
    build's configuration and license information.

    Draftcut invokes ffmpeg and ffprobe as separate processes. It does not link
    the libav* libraries (no ctypes, cffi, PyAV or ffmpeg-python) and does not
    bundle an ffmpeg binary; you install it yourself.

    If you redistribute an ffmpeg binary together with Draftcut, that
    distribution carries the obligations of that ffmpeg build's license (GPL if
    it is a GPL build). The current encoding paths require libx264, a GPL
    component; an LGPL-only build without it cannot run those paths unchanged.

Model weights:
  No model weights are included in this source tree. The distribution gitignore
  excludes mlx_models/; model downloads and caches may use other locations.
  Models used for speech transcription are downloaded separately and are
  governed by their own licenses.

